            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 80-year-old female admitted on 01/12/2017 with an acute exacerbation of her known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD). On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray and arterial blood gas analysis were performed confirming exacerbation without pneumonic consolidation. Spirometry confirmed severely reduced airflow. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), a course of systemic corticosteroids (prednisolone), and supplemental oxygen therapy. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. She was discharged on 02/12/2017 in stable condition. Discharge medications include inhaled bronchodilators and a tapering oral steroid course. Please arrange early follow-up and review of her long-term COPD management plan. Do not hesitate to contact me with any queries.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
